# Task 6 Fix Round 1 Re-review

**Base:** `458ba55`  
**Head:** `5cebaf9`  
**Verdict:** **NEEDS FIXES — Critical 2, Important 1, Minor 2**

## Scope and method

This was a fresh read-only review of the full Fix Round 1 section of `task-6-report.md`, the full supplied `review-458ba55..5cebaf9.diff`, the Task 6 brief, the relevant approved-design sections, current code, and focused tests. No tracked file was edited. No provider, network, live-pricing, real-SDK, replay, Docker, background process, or permanent ledger was used. The only execution beyond read-only inspection was one pure in-process pricing reproducer.

The ordinary-path fixes are substantial, but the two Critical boundaries are still live-object checks rather than checks over the exact bytes/rates later consumed. The all-exit fix also unlocks the authorization lease before terminal audit/closure is durable, so a crash or persistent audit failure can permit a later planned call after a terminal outcome.

